A library.

A book has a title (text), an author (text) and a loaned (yes or no).

A shelf (a list of books) is all loaned when:
the book's loaned for every book in the shelf.

A shelf (a list of books) has something by an author (text) when:
the book's author is the author for some book in the shelf.

Suppose dune is a book with title "Dune", author "Herbert" and loaned true.
Suppose emma is a book with title "Emma", author "Austen" and loaned false.
For example, a list of dune and emma is not all loaned.
For example, a list of dune is all loaned.
For example, a list of dune and emma has something by "Austen".
For example, a list of dune has something by "Austen" is false.
